Exact machine-registry snapshot for self-contained planning: registries/claims.toml
Header: {"revision":1,"schema":"fdgr.claims.v1"}
Each row is binding input to WP-000 and its owning work packages. If the source registry changes, update the affected C01/V04/Q05 beads and this snapshot before implementation; compact prose cannot weaken a row.
- CLAIM-RAW-001: {"id":"CLAIM-RAW-001","name":"Original bytes retained","required_evidence":["raw_object_digest","source_receipt","local_retrieval_verification"],"terminal_predicate":"The exact acquired byte range can be read back and hashes to the declared identity."}
- CLAIM-TIME-001: {"id":"CLAIM-TIME-001","name":"Frame timeline continuous","required_evidence":["packet_timeline","decode_timeline","discontinuity_scan","clock_model"],"terminal_predicate":"Every accepted frame is mapped to a named clock epoch with bounded residual and all gaps are explicit."}
- CLAIM-CAL-001: {"id":"CLAIM-CAL-001","name":"Camera calibration admitted","required_evidence":["calibration_basis","reprojection_corpus","distortion_policy","temperature_or_zoom_scope"],"terminal_predicate":"Calibration residuals satisfy the registered scope-specific gate and the lens state matches the capture."}
- CLAIM-POSE-001: {"id":"CLAIM-POSE-001","name":"Camera pose generation admitted","required_evidence":["anchor","pose_graph","reprojection_receipt","trajectory_diagnostics","decision_certificate"],"terminal_predicate":"The pose graph is connected for the claimed domain, finite, deterministic, and passes residual and loop-consistency gates."}
- CLAIM-SCALE-001: {"id":"CLAIM-SCALE-001","name":"Metric scale witnessed","required_evidence":["scale_witness","transform","residuals","scope","independence_class"],"terminal_predicate":"A registered witness establishes the metric transform within its declared uncertainty and domain."}
- CLAIM-GEO-001: {"id":"CLAIM-GEO-001","name":"Surface geometry admitted","required_evidence":["pose_generation","depth_or_correspondence_evidence","fusion_receipt","uncertainty_field","coverage_certificate"],"terminal_predicate":"Published geometry reconstructs held-out observations within the gate and carries spatial uncertainty and coverage."}
- CLAIM-SEM-001: {"id":"CLAIM-SEM-001","name":"Semantic asset resolved","required_evidence":["ontology_version","multi_view_observations","geometry_association","resolver_policy","counterevidence_scan"],"terminal_predicate":"The asset satisfies the ontology-specific resolution gate and all supporting observations remain valid at the anchor."}
- CLAIM-ABS-001: {"id":"CLAIM-ABS-001","name":"Asset absent from domain","required_evidence":["authorized_domain","coverage_certificate","detectability_model","negative_search_receipt"],"terminal_predicate":"The complete claimed domain was observed with sufficient detectability and yielded no qualifying observation."}
- CLAIM-ARCH-001: {"id":"CLAIM-ARCH-001","name":"Cloud replica retrievable","required_evidence":["upload_manifest","provider_receipt","head_receipt","sampled_or_full_readback","digest_verification"],"terminal_predicate":"The object graph can be retrieved from the declared provider and independently reconstructs the published root."}
- CLAIM-READY-001: {"id":"CLAIM-READY-001","name":"Digital twin release qualified","required_evidence":["all_child_claims","compatibility_profile","privacy_receipt","benchmark_receipt","recovery_drill"],"terminal_predicate":"Every advertised readiness dimension has a current positive evidence receipt and no blocking negative evidence."}

