Each row is binding input to WP-000 and its owning work packages. If the source registry changes, update the affected C01/V04/Q05 beads and this snapshot before implementation; compact prose cannot weaken a row.
- GATE-000: {"id":"GATE-000","name":"Constitution frozen","terminal_predicate":"Registries parse, stable IDs are unique, dependency policy passes, and no implementation claim exceeds evidence."}
- GATE-001: {"id":"GATE-001","name":"Reference identity and ledger","terminal_predicate":"Canonical codec and single-threaded ledger replay byte-identically across the fixture corpus."}
- GATE-002: {"id":"GATE-002","name":"Crash-safe evidence publication","terminal_predicate":"Original media and evidence roots survive the complete staged-publication crash matrix."}
- GATE-003: {"id":"GATE-003","name":"Media normalization qualified","terminal_predicate":"Sidecar cancellation, malformed media, timestamp accounting, deterministic profiles, and output verification pass."}
- GATE-004: {"id":"GATE-004","name":"Calibration and scale honest","terminal_predicate":"Metric exports are impossible without scale witnesses; calibration and scale uncertainty calibrate on held-out fixtures."}
- GATE-005: {"id":"GATE-005","name":"Recorded capture useful","terminal_predicate":"At least one DJI Flip recorded path and one generic camera path produce complete anchored frame generations."}
- GATE-006: {"id":"GATE-006","name":"Live observation admitted","terminal_predicate":"A version-pinned owner-authorized live path runs read-only, accounts for gaps, and closes without leaked work or secrets."}
- GATE-007: {"id":"GATE-007","name":"Reference geometry oracle","terminal_predicate":"A deterministic classical baseline produces poses and sparse geometry with known failure classifications."}
- GATE-008: {"id":"GATE-008","name":"Model lanes admitted","terminal_predicate":"Exact model artifacts pass license, sandbox, schema, numeric, reproducibility, and domain benchmark gates."}
- GATE-009: {"id":"GATE-009","name":"Refined geometry stable","terminal_predicate":"Pose and depth refinement outperform or safely reject priors without nondeterministic publication drift."}
- GATE-010: {"id":"GATE-010","name":"Digital surface model useful","terminal_predicate":"Fused geometry, uncertainty, coverage, held-out reprojection, scale, and topology metrics meet profile targets."}
- GATE-011: {"id":"GATE-011","name":"Semantic twin trustworthy","terminal_predicate":"Ontology assets resolve with evidence, counterevidence, critical-asset review, and calibrated uncertainty."}
- GATE-012: {"id":"GATE-012","name":"Archive recoverable","terminal_predicate":"Local loss followed by B2 or R2 restore reconstructs every retained authoritative root from verified objects."}
- GATE-013: {"id":"GATE-013","name":"Human and agent surfaces complete","terminal_predicate":"CLI, reports, search, measurements, and exports preserve anchors, status, uncertainty, and stable schemas."}
- GATE-014: {"id":"GATE-014","name":"Agent integration non-bypassable","terminal_predicate":"MCP and Eidetic surfaces cannot mutate or redefine canonical state outside registered semantic paths."}
- GATE-015: {"id":"GATE-015","name":"Fault and benchmark evidence","terminal_predicate":"Lab schedules and ground-truth campaigns cover named failure classes with reproducible receipts."}
- GATE-016: {"id":"GATE-016","name":"Performance claims earned","terminal_predicate":"Same-binary experiments show semantic equivalence and statistically defensible latency, cost, and memory results."}
- GATE-017: {"id":"GATE-017","name":"Release qualified","terminal_predicate":"All advertised platform, device, model, privacy, recovery, and performance dimensions have current positive evidence."}
- GATE-018: {"id":"GATE-018","name":"Agent semantics contract locked","terminal_predicate":"The abstraction tower, operating loop, anchor vector, four ledgers, epistemic lattice, question graph, Agent Turn Packet, profiles, and authority boundaries have machine contracts and golden vectors."}
- GATE-019: {"id":"GATE-019","name":"Cold orientation and context packs qualified","terminal_predicate":"Cold arrival, pulse, briefing, tactical, forensic, budget, gap, and Pack DNA scenarios satisfy determinism, sufficiency, coverage, and token-economy tests."}
- GATE-020: {"id":"GATE-020","name":"Question-driven planning qualified","terminal_predicate":"Objectives, questions, deficits, affordances, candidate plans, Pareto comparison, value-of-information, and stopping rules replay deterministically and never bypass authority."}
- GATE-021: {"id":"GATE-021","name":"Active work and handoff qualified","terminal_predicate":"Obligations, semantic progress, confirmations, indeterminate effects, cancellation, reconciliation, and handoff/resume remain sufficient across context and agent replacement."}
- GATE-022: {"id":"GATE-022","name":"Accretion qualified","terminal_predicate":"Episodes, surprises, cost calibration, feedback, lesson promotion, shadow/canary policy, monitoring, and rollback improve qualified workloads without weakening proof gates."}
- GATE-023: {"id":"GATE-023","name":"Agent-native release qualified","terminal_predicate":"Self-description, first-try discoverability, live/lab adapter parity, multi-agent coordination, and the full orient-to-handoff loop pass local Doodlestein qualification on advertised profiles."}
- GATE-024: {"id":"GATE-024","name":"Shared cockpit and pilot protocol qualified","terminal_predicate":"Decision Frames, epistemic-debt attention, frame-complete spatial handles, and human-pilot cards pass semantic-equivalence, cold-resume, stability, access-control, cognitive-load, stop, refusal, and abort campaigns."}

