Exact machine-registry snapshot for self-contained planning: registries/open_questions.toml
Header: {"revision":1,"schema":"fdgr.open_questions.v1"}
Each row is binding input to WP-000 and its owning work packages. If the source registry changes, update the affected C01/V04/Q05 beads and this snapshot before implementation; compact prose cannot weaken a row.
- OPEN-001: {"id":"OPEN-001","name":"Canonical internal world frame","statement":"Should the default local world be gravity-aligned ENU, a camera-origin similarity frame, or a building-aligned frame with explicit transform? Decision requires telemetry availability, interchange needs, numeric stability, and repeated-capture alignment tests."}
- OPEN-002: {"id":"OPEN-002","name":"Canonical binary codec","statement":"Use a fully custom compact codec, a tightly specified subset of an existing format, or an owned Franken codec? Need independent implementation, evolution, zero-copy potential, bounds, and audit."}
- OPEN-003: {"id":"OPEN-003","name":"Logical versus representation identity","statement":"How should exact logical media identity relate to different chunk/compression/encryption representations while preserving verification and deduplication?"}
- OPEN-004: {"id":"OPEN-004","name":"Best analysis mezzanine","statement":"All-intra AV1/HEVC, FFV1, JPEG XL/PNG frame sequence, or multiple profiles? Measure decode random access, determinism, quality, storage, and model throughput."}
- OPEN-005: {"id":"OPEN-005","name":"DJI telemetry availability","statement":"Which exact Flip original files, app exports, controller sessions, or private protocols expose camera/gimbal/GNSS/barometer telemetry, at what rate/clock/accuracy? Unknown until measured by profile."}
- OPEN-006: {"id":"OPEN-006","name":"Model execution portability","statement":"Container, Python environment lock, Nix/OCI, uv, or custom artifact bundle? Need offline, reproducible GPU profiles without expanding the Rust trust domain."}
- OPEN-007: {"id":"OPEN-007","name":"Geometry canonical representation","statement":"Should surfels, TSDF/occupancy tiles, or another probabilistic surface be the primary canonical fused representation? Decision should optimize validation, incremental update, measurements, semantics, storage, and export rather than rendering fashion."}
- OPEN-008: {"id":"OPEN-008","name":"Uncertainty representation","statement":"Full covariance, diagonal/local approximations, ensembles, evidential distributions, spatial error bounds, or multiple typed fields? Need calibration and computational feasibility."}
- OPEN-009: {"id":"OPEN-009","name":"Cross-capture registration","statement":"How should repeated captures align under seasonal change, moved objects, new calibration, and weak geodetic priors while distinguishing physical change from model reinterpretation?"}
- OPEN-010: {"id":"OPEN-010","name":"Semantic ontology granularity","statement":"How fine should utility/equipment taxonomy become before data and resolution gates support it? Too coarse is not useful; too fine invites hallucinated specificity."}
- OPEN-011: {"id":"OPEN-011","name":"Human confirmation UX","statement":"Which evidence views and questions let an owner confirm an asset accurately with minimal burden? How is reviewer uncertainty represented?"}
- OPEN-012: {"id":"OPEN-012","name":"Agent query language","statement":"Typed JSON AST first is safe; when does a textual query language produce enough token/usability benefit to justify a parser/optimizer?"}
- OPEN-013: {"id":"OPEN-013","name":"Archive transport implementation","statement":"Asupersync-native HTTP/TLS/S3 in Rust versus tightly scoped process sidecar versus ATP gateway. The choice must satisfy closed-dependency, credential, cancellation, performance, and portability requirements."}
- OPEN-014: {"id":"OPEN-014","name":"RaptorQ allocation policy","statement":"Which object classes and repair ratios minimize expected loss/retrieval cost under local/B2/R2 failure models?"}
- OPEN-015: {"id":"OPEN-015","name":"Safe public sharing","statement":"Can useful geometry/coverage reports be shared while removing location, textures, neighboring property, and critical assets? Need measurable re-identification/privacy tests."}
- OPEN-016: {"id":"OPEN-016","name":"Live model architecture","statement":"DA3 Streaming, CUT3R, another successor, or a classical/learned hybrid? Exact decision should be renewed at implementation time using current primary sources and FDGR benchmarks."}
- OPEN-017: {"id":"OPEN-017","name":"Pure-Rust media hot paths","statement":"Which demux/decode/image operations are worth owning in safe Rust after profiling, and which remain best isolated in ffmpeg?"}
- OPEN-018: {"id":"OPEN-018","name":"Formal methods scope","statement":"Which state machines merit TLA+/Lean/model checking first: publication, idempotency/effect reconciliation, archive deletion, capability noninterference, or scale/claim transitions?"}
- OPEN-019: {"id":"OPEN-019","name":"Question graph granularity","statement":"Which questions should be durable nodes versus ephemeral compiler artifacts, and how can FDGR avoid both hidden uncertainty and excessive ceremony?"}
- OPEN-020: {"id":"OPEN-020","name":"Context-pack objective","statement":"Which deterministic submodular objective and mandatory classes best predict agent decision quality per token across geometry, capture, archive, and semantic tasks?"}
- OPEN-021: {"id":"OPEN-021","name":"Recommendation utility representation","statement":"How should lexicographic safety constraints, Pareto frontiers, calibrated costs, value of information, and user preference combine without an opaque scalar?"}
- OPEN-022: {"id":"OPEN-022","name":"Episode causal evidence","statement":"Which interventions and natural experiments are sufficient to promote capture, model-selection, or budgeting lessons without mistaking correlation for causation?"}
- OPEN-023: {"id":"OPEN-023","name":"Multi-agent branch economics","statement":"When do branch-per-agent and shared question bundles reduce total work enough to justify their metadata and merge cost?"}
- OPEN-024: {"id":"OPEN-024","name":"Pilot guidance presentation","statement":"What is the lowest-cognitive-load visual and textual guidance that helps a human obtain the requested view without implying unsupported autonomous control?"}
- OPEN-025: {"id":"OPEN-025","name":"Agent ergonomics benchmark","statement":"Which cold-arrival, context-loss, uncertainty, error, and handoff scenarios best measure first-try success, decision quality, and total control cost across frontier agents?"}
- OPEN-026: {"id":"OPEN-026","question":"What Decision Frame density maximizes first-turn decision success across model context sizes without hiding meaningful alternatives?"}
- OPEN-027: {"id":"OPEN-027","question":"Which visual, spoken, haptic, or controller-overlay pilot-card modalities minimize operator load for each admitted DJI profile?"}
- OPEN-028: {"id":"OPEN-028","question":"How should epistemic-debt loss and question-sharing value be calibrated without allowing adaptive policy to suppress safety-critical uncertainty?"}

