- SLO-001: {"id":"SLO-001","name":"Capture accounting","statement":"Every admitted source byte/packet/frame range is either published, explicitly rejected, or represented as a gap; unaccounted loss is zero."}
- SLO-002: {"id":"SLO-002","name":"Online feedback","statement":"On a qualified workstation profile, p95 source-frame-to-quality/coverage update is under 2 seconds and progress heartbeat under 500 ms, excluding known source latency. Geometry may be slower and explicitly stale."}
- SLO-003: {"id":"SLO-003","name":"Publication atomicity","statement":"Across the complete kill-point campaign, readers observe only the prior or successor complete root; zero partial roots."}
- SLO-004: {"id":"SLO-004","name":"Cancellation","statement":"Cooperative local work stops accepting new effects immediately and reaches terminal or explicit indeterminate state within the profile drain budget; zero silent descendants or lost obligations."}
- SLO-005: {"id":"SLO-005","name":"Exterior geometry standard profile","statement":"On the ground-truth home corpus under a defined capture protocol and witnessed scale, visible static surface median error ≤ 5 cm, 90th percentile ≤ 15 cm, and certifiable surface completeness ≥ 90%, with calibrated uncertainty and named excluded materials/regions."}
- SLO-006: {"id":"SLO-006","name":"High-quality profile","statement":"Under closer/slower capture and stronger calibration/scale evidence, visible static surface median error ≤ 2.5 cm and selected opening/asset dimension median error ≤ 3 cm on qualified corpora. This is not a universal product promise."}
- SLO-007: {"id":"SLO-007","name":"Critical semantic precision","statement":"Resolved critical-asset false-positive rate below 1% on the qualification corpus, using abstention/human confirmation as needed. Hypothesis recall is measured separately."}
- SLO-008: {"id":"SLO-008","name":"Archive recovery","statement":"A full local-loss restore from each advertised provider reconstructs every retained root with byte-identical object identities and zero silent substitution."}
- SLO-009: {"id":"SLO-009","name":"Deterministic reference replay","statement":"Strict reference state machines, plans, manifests, claims, and reports reproduce byte-identically across qualified platforms where specified."}
- SLO-010: {"id":"SLO-010","name":"Agent economy","statement":"Representative “what is missing?”, “why this asset?”, “measure this opening,” and “verify archive” workflows complete with bounded context packs and an order of magnitude fewer transferred tokens than raw frame/point dumps."}
- SLO-011: {"id":"SLO-011","name":"Cold-agent orientation","statement":"A qualified cold-arrival scenario identifies the current mission, exact anchor/continuity, top world facts, highest-value unresolved questions, all critical active work, authority posture, and safest next step from one briefing response."}
- SLO-012: {"id":"SLO-012","name":"Heartbeat economy","statement":"When no meaningful change occurs, p95 pulse output is at most 400 tokens and contains no unchanged inventory while preserving continuity, active indeterminate work, and critical warnings."}
- SLO-013: {"id":"SLO-013","name":"Context value density","statement":"On the agent benchmark suite, context-pack selection achieves at least the decision success of the full eligible context with at most one tenth of transferred tokens for representative bounded tasks."}
- SLO-014: {"id":"SLO-014","name":"Handoff sufficiency","statement":"A fresh agent resumes and completes the minimum safe next step from the handoff capsule alone in every qualified handoff scenario, without replaying the prior transcript."}
- SLO-015: {"id":"SLO-015","name":"Recommendation calibration","statement":"Predicted information gain, resource cost, and completion interval are calibrated by workload class and expose drift before policy promotion."}
- SLO-016: {"id":"SLO-016","name":"First-try discoverability","statement":"At least 95% of canonical benchmark intents map to a valid read/propose path on the first call using only self-description, and every rejected attempt names an exact safe repair."}
- SLO-017: {"id":"SLO-017","name":"Accretive control cost","statement":"For repeated qualified workload classes, admitted learning reduces median total control cost without regression in proof, calibration, safety, or recovery gates; gains are receipt-scoped rather than assumed."}
- SLO-018: {"id":"SLO-018","name":"Decision Frame sufficiency","statement":"A qualified decision scenario can be correctly continued from its Decision Frame and referenced expansions without joining unrelated responses or replaying the transcript."}
- SLO-019: {"id":"SLO-019","name":"Attention stability","statement":"Unchanged or immaterially changed attention items do not re-interrupt the agent; every repeated foreground item cites a material transition or expired acknowledgement."}
- SLO-020: {"id":"SLO-020","name":"Pilot cognitive economy","statement":"Normal pilot guidance presents one primary card with at most two short cues, names done/abort conditions, and improves useful evidence per operator minute without increasing safety-preemption failures."}

